adr: 0229
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: dump-dispatch
why: A case label may be a *range*, and every constant in it is named. Counting one per range answers 2 of 5 where a `red..green` arm and a `blue` arm name 3, so a case that covers its enumeration through ranges reads as a subset and one that names a subset reads as smaller still. Every count in the catalogue would move at once, which is the loudest possible failure -- and a corpus whose labels are all single constants would not notice at all, which is why tests/dumps/dispatch.pas has a range in it.
--- old
      disp^.named := disp^.named + r^.hi - r^.lo + 1;
--- new
      disp^.named := disp^.named + 1;
